		<notes>
			<note>Withy advertised and sold a card with twelve rules for whist on one side and an advertisement for his brokerage business on the other. I have elected to treat the whist rules as the recto. </note>
			<note rend="paragraph"/>
			<note>In 1785, Withy expanded the twelve rules to twenty four as </note>
			<note url="withy.whist.b.1.xml">Withy.Whist.B.1</note>
			<note>. In 1791, he produced a much-expanded
				chapbook version of the rules with added laws and odds as </note>
			<note url="withy.whist.c.1.xml">Withy.Whist.C.1</note>
			<note>.</note>
